l we see  from the president as far as strategy  with 11 days left well you heard the  president say that last night he said  i'm not a politician  that's why i won in 2016. and he said i  i ran for president because of the  failed policies  of career politicians like you joe biden  i mean he literally said  that to uh to joe biden last night so i  i do think you're going to hear the  president echo that message he's been  saying it he continues to say  i have done more in 47 months than joe  biden has done  in 47 years uh but look it's it's also  about reminding people  what the accomplishments of this  president actually are so that's why  we're spread out sandra all across the  country our entire family  including the president vice president  we're out there reminding the american  people  what this president has been able to  deliver in record time  and why he is the only person that can  bring this economy back and get us to  those great heights that we saw not too  many months ago laura one of the biggest  moments of the night last night was when  the two  had this exchange over the coronavirus  and handling the pandemic watch  anyone who's responsible for that many  deaths should not remain as president of  the united states of america  we're in a situation where there are a  thousand deaths a day  now it will go away and as i say we're  rounding the turn we're rounding the  corner it's going away  johns hopkins university reports that  the seven day rolling average of new  cases in this country  is up 18 000 in just the last week laura  daly new deaths is up 9  you just heard the president make as  while joe biden painted a picture of  what he said could be a very dark winter  for this country  so did it help for the president to take  that approach considering  joe biden still is polling above the  president  on american voters and who they think is  best to handle this pandemic  well look at the onset of this we saw  that the predictions were that we could  see upwards  of two million deaths now one death is  too many our hearts go out to everyone  who's had to deal with this  but the president took on a novel virus  something we had  never seen before anywhere in the world  and so this was historic what this  president did not only  with testing with ventilators partnering  with the private sector  paycheck protection program now we are  on the precipice of a vaccine  in record time so when that happens i  think we're going to see a huge  change across the country and the  president has said that is probably  weeks away i think it's a terrible  message to send to the american people  that you heard from joe biden  that it would be a dark winter why would  we want to be so negative and dismal  that's very  very disturbing to hear you want a  president who's positive who's uplifting  who knows what's on the horizon as  president trump does with this vaccine  and i think we're going to see a big  change when that comes out quick  follow-up on that  we saw you as well as the president's  children walk into the debate hall  last night wearing masks you sat down  you wore them the whole time  was that a change in heart over wearing  the mask or was that because  the debate commission made that a rule  well that that's because they asked us  to wear the mask the whole time  again i continue to reiterate that the  first time around that was not  made you know perfectly clear to us we  walked in with them and we thought we  were okay to take them off when we sat  down  happy to keep them on if that was the  rule and that's what we did lara final  question on  women voters and we can put up on the  screen this is our new  fox news state polling on joe biden  and how he's polling versus the  president with suburban women  you can clearly see that joe biden is  running up the score among suburban  women  this concern the campaign and what are  you doing in the final days to try to  change some of those minds well look we  have